# Build context for deploy/daemon/Dockerfile is the repository root
# (deploy/runner/docker-compose.yml: context ../..). Without this file every
# build streamed node_modules, .git, secrets/, certs/, data/ and the runner's
# .env (VNC password) to the Docker daemon, and a `COPY . .` added later would
# have baked them into the image.
#
# Allowlist rather than blocklist: the Dockerfile copies exactly package.json,
# package-lock.json, src/ and daemon/, so everything else is excluded by the
# first line and only those four are let back in. Adding a COPY to the
# Dockerfile means adding a `!` line here, or the build fails visibly with
# "not found", which is the wanted failure mode.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!src
!daemon

# Inside the allowed directories: the hub's runtime state (pairing tokens,
# replay nonces) must never reach an image, and neither must editor litter or
# documentation the process does not read.
daemon/data
**/state.json
**/state.json.tmp
**/*.md
**/.DS_Store
